-- title:
--   Diamond group over X₀(Mp) has order [(ℤ/M)^×:± 1]
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a positive integer $M$ with $M \ge 5$ and $p \nmid M$, and a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, together with a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K_1, K_2$ be intermediate fields of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ with $K_2 \le K_1$, where $K_1$ is `laurentBaseChange` of `x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ M p`, that is, the field generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by all quotients of $q$-expansion series attached to modular forms of equal weight for $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$ having integral $q$-expansions (nonzero denominator), and $K_2$ is the analogous base change of the corresponding $q$-expansion field for $\Gamma_0(Mp)$. Let $G$ be a finite group acting on $K_1$ by ring and semiring automorphisms, faithfully, such that every $g \in G$ fixes each element of $K_1$ lying in $K_2$, and conversely every element of $K_1$ fixed by all of $G$ lies in $K_2$. Then the cardinality of $G$ equals the index of the subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M\mathbb{Z})^\times$ generated by $-1$.
--
--   The group $G$ is the group of diamond operators $\langle d \rangle$, $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M\mathbb{Z})^\times/\{\pm 1\}$, realised abstractly as a faithful finite automorphism group of the function field of $X(\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p))$ with fixed field that of $X_0(Mp)$; the conclusion computes its order as $\varphi(M)/2$. It feeds the dictionary between inertia at supersingular points of the two-chart integral model and stabilisers of level structures, used in the analysis of the cover $X(\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)) \to X_0(Mp)$.
